# Manual Chunk Quality Review

## Fixed-size Chunk Review

| Chunk | Observation | Problem Identified |
|---|---|---|
| Fixed_001 | Starts with one article and continues into another | Article boundary divided |
| Fixed_015 | Contains two different legal topics | Unrelated provisions combined |
| Fixed_030 | Article heading separated from text | Lost legal context |
| Fixed_045 | Sentence continues from previous chunk | Requires overlap |
| Fixed_060 | Contains mixed provisions | Reduced retrieval accuracy |

Result:

Fixed-size chunking creates technically valid chunks but does not preserve legal meaning.

Decision:

Reject.

---

## Paragraph-based Chunk Review

| Chunk | Observation | Problem Identified |
|---|---|---|
| Paragraph_001 | Paragraph structure preserved | Good |
| Paragraph_012 | OCR merged paragraphs | Incorrect boundary |
| Paragraph_025 | Heading separated from paragraph | Metadata issue |
| Paragraph_040 | Contains multiple legal ideas | Less precise retrieval |
| Paragraph_055 | Paragraph too large | Retrieval noise |

Result:

Paragraph chunking performs better than fixed-size but depends heavily on OCR quality.

Decision:

Reject.

