# Conclusion

The experiment demonstrated that legal structure-based chunking provides the best approach for Ethiopian legal documents.

Fixed-size chunking produced consistent chunks but ignored legal boundaries.

Paragraph-based chunking preserved local context but was affected by OCR formatting issues.

Legal structure-based chunking preserved article-level meaning, maintained metadata relationships, and improved retrieval suitability.

Therefore, legal structure-based chunking was selected as the final chunking strategy for the Ethiopian Legal Semantic Retrieval System.